[38;2;124;124;124mwritable ordinals, and Σ is the supremum of accidentally writable ordinals.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow, **iterated ITTMs**: The idea is to consider ITTMs with oracles. If we give [0m[38;2;124;124;124man ITTM an oracle for a real, it can write more ordinals. The "λ-jump" or [0m
[38;2;124;124;124miteration process:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mStarting with λ₀ = λ (the supremum of writable ordinals by ordinary ITTMs), we [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcan define:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- λ₁ = the supremum of ordinals writable by an ITTM with oracle for a code of λ₀[0m[38;2;124;124;124m- And so on...[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, I think the iterated ITTM hierarchy relates to the concept of "Σ₂¹-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mreflecting ordinals" through the connection between ITTMs and descriptive set [0m
