[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about the connection to Σ₂¹-reflecting ordinals.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mA Σ₂¹-reflecting ordinal is an ordinal α such that for every Σ₂¹ formula φ, if [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mL_α ⊨ φ then there exists β < α with L_β ⊨ φ. Actually, more precisely, α is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mΣ_n^1-reflecting if L_α ≺_{Σ_n^1} V (or equivalently, L_α reflects Σ_n^1 [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mformulas).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWait, I need to be more careful. The notion of Π_n^1-reflecting or Σ_n^1-[0m
